        "spya-kmgwhs",
        "spya-tz99zn"
      ],
      "title": "Data type and sample size",
      "gist": "Different redundancy functions suit discrete, Gaussian, or mixed continuous data differently, and because joint probability distributions grow exponentially with the number of variables, undersampling can severely distort results."
    },
